  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B046 joins a clear biological and technological principle to long-established prevention of infection and related cancers. Its medical significance is exceptional, its effects are mature at population scale, and Lowy, Frazer, and Schiller provide a coherent three-person attribution spanning the vaccine concept and its realization.",
    "case_against": "The experimental and translational history encompasses further important contributors, so the relative allocation of credit among foundational papillomavirus biology, particle design, and vaccine development remains the principal reservation.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "sandberg-rickard",
        "point": "Sandberg ranked B009 first because antisense correction of SMN2 splicing is a mechanistically precise and clinically consequential treatment for a severe inherited disease.",
        "response": "I agree that B009 is an unusually compelling demonstration of RNA biology translated into patient benefit and retain it as an alternative. I nevertheless give B046 priority because prevention of infection-associated cancers has broader, longer-established public-health reach, while the boundary between foundational splicing work and therapeutic-platform credit in B009 warrants further scrutiny."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius ranked B004 first, emphasizing the broad clinical consequences of GLP-1 physiology and therapies for diabetes and obesity.",
        "response": "The maturity and medical importance of B004 are undeniable. However, its four credited names and the difficult division between incretin physiology, peptide biology, and medicine development make the three available places particularly consequential; B046 presently offers the more delimited attribution alongside comparable maturity and extraordinary preventive benefit."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the candidate record supports a sufficiently precise division of credit among the distinct scientific and translational stages of HPV vaccine development.",
      "Whether B004's attribution can be resolved fairly within three laureate places."
